    "confidence": "high",
    "rationale": "PathSpec.match_file currently forwards to self._match_file and returns the 'include' value directly, which is Optional[bool]. When no patterns match, include can be None, causing match_file() to return None. The GitIgnoreSpec._match_file implementation explicitly returns Tuple[Optional[bool], Optional[int]] and sets out_include default to None. Therefore the fix should be in PathSpec.match_file to coerce None to False. I selected pathspec/pathspec.py as the source to edit, and tests/test_03_pathspec.py as the location to add a regression test verifying match_file() returns False when no patterns match.",
    "evidence": [
      {
        "path": "pathspec/pathspec.py",
        "detail": "PathSpec.match_file returns include directly (lines ~278-280 and ~318-320). _match_file is assigned to util.check_match_file by default; include can be Optional[bool]."
      },
      {
        "path": "pathspec/gitignore.py",
        "detail": "GitIgnoreSpec._match_file returns Tuple[Optional[bool], Optional[int]] and sets out_include default to None; if no pattern matched it returns (None, None). (lines ~107-157)"
      }
    ],
